Alembic migrations for the Sajilo Sewa backend.

DATABASE_URL is read from the environment (.env) by alembic/env.py — do not
hardcode it in alembic.ini.

Common commands (run from server/):
  alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe change"   # generate a new migration after editing app/models
  alembic upgrade head                                    # apply all pending migrations
  alembic downgrade -1                                    # roll back one migration
  alembic current                                         # show current DB revision

After autogenerating a migration, always review the generated upgrade()/
downgrade() before applying it — autogenerate can miss things like data
backfills, check constraints, or column renames (it will see a rename as a
drop + add).
